:{"fieldSizeRank":2,"finishersRank":1,"finishRateRank":71,"winningTimeRank":9,"winningTimeRankDir":3,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["up"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:26:25","holder":"Dmitri GRISHIN","year":1998,"type":"up"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1959,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"06:28:11"}},"narrative":"The 2000 Comrades Marathon was the 75th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 87.300 km. The race was held on Friday, 16 June. Conditions: Warm sunny day. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nVladimir KOTOV claimed the men's title in 05:25:33, ahead of Alexei Volgin (05:27:08) and Dmitri GRISHIN (05:32:47). Maria BAK won the women's race in 06:15:35, followed by Birgit LENNARTZ (06:33:55).\n\nVladimir KOTOV's 05:25:33 set a new up record, beating Dmitri GRISHIN's 05:26:25 from 1998. Maria BAK's 06:15:35 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1959 (Trevor ALLEN, 06:28:11).\n\nFrom a field of 24,523 entries, 19,988 runners crossed the finish line (81.5% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 16,693 men and 3,295 women (16.5% female). The average finish time was 10:19:13.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 694 Silver, 3,279 Bill Rowan, 15,992 Bronze, 3 Vic Clapham. 6,795 runners (34.0%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Tsombere Zakariya TSHANKIE in 12:00:00.\n\nThis edition featured the 2nd largest field in race history and the 1st most finishers ever. Compared to the previous up run in 1998, the field was 83.4% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 42% of the finishers, with 11,577 seniors (avg 10:13:08) and 8,411 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}